# clean-chat

Same product as convex-chat, different architecture. Read `AGENTS.md`. Behavior: `docs/PRODUCT.md`. Layers: `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`.

- npm workspaces: `@clean-chat/core` → `application` → `infrastructure`; `@clean-chat/client` → `core`; `@clean-chat/web` → `client` + `core`
- Dependencies point inward. Core imports nothing except TypeBox. Infrastructure may import inner packages. Client may import core only (not application or infrastructure). Web may import client and core only. Never the reverse.
- One domain concept per folder under `packages/core/src/domain`. Schema first: `XxxSchema` with TypeBox, then `type Xxx = Static<typeof XxxSchema>`. No classes. Domain must not import use-cases or events.
- Driving contract (`UseCase` I/O via `@clean-chat/core/use-cases`; `AppEvent`, `EventSubscriber` from `@clean-chat/core`). Driven ports and interactors live in `@clean-chat/application`.
- Use cases are `UseCase<Input, Output>` with a readonly `name` (HTTP path). One `execute` is one `UnitOfWork.run`. Persistence methods take `TransactionContext`. Publish `AppEvent` after commit. The UI listens with `EventSubscriber`. HTTP binds the actor from `Authorization: Bearer`. Input is checked by a pluggable `InputValidator` (default TypeBox `Value.Check`) before `execute`. Known errors map to 401/403/400; SSE requires a session.
- Preserve JSDoc on public types, ports, and use-case functions.
- Do not add DMs, file uploads, Clerk, Next.js, a router, or password-reset email unless requested
- Persistence is in-memory (`@clean-chat/infrastructure` `src/memory/`). Do not pick a SQL database or auth library until that layer is being discussed. The UI is Vite + React in `@clean-chat/web`.
- Do not copy Convex `api.*`, `useQuery`, or `_id` / `_creationTime` into the domain
